    {
      "question": "e-6566",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "49c811596348972dc68ac6f1cbaf0f786ea8e0e88de62a7bfaa2a3717919ae5c",
      "new_sha256": "bae42fa144159ebfbcbed9a019d90427e8c562512e60d2c9793299cc7237969c",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-6566",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "A second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x)y'' + b(x)y' + c(x) y = f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\ny'' + (y-1)y'+x = 2\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $(y-1)y'.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\ny''+y'=x \\cos x\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x) = 1, b(x) = 1, c(x) = 0,$ and $f(x) = x\\cos{x}.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\nyy'' - y'+ 9 = 0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $yy''.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/example-6566.json",
          "file_sha256": "b5a37b22782d16ea63998bb6d506138cf1ce6ed238e9adb8148b0010e5973e9b"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1967,
